<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2">
  <Document>
    <name>🌊 LIVE WAVE HEIGHT</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<p><b>Legend</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/wave_height/legend.png?v=glwu-20261010-1300Z-r12" width="600" alt="legend"><br>Every pixel shows its bin's exact color; the legend is the full table. Unwritten rules: <b>0 and 0.1 ft</b> show as <b>0 ft</b>; <b>0.2 to 0.6 ft</b> show as <b>0.5 ft</b>; <b>0.7 to 1 ft</b> show as <b>1-2 ft</b>. Each 2-ft label covers its full step up to the next row (e.g. the 4-5 ft color covers 4 up to 6 ft), so every value lands in exactly one color. Model maximum this run: <b>8.5 ft</b>. Values above 30 ft stay white. Significant height = average of highest third of waves. For more precise wave height data, turn on the NOAA Great Lakes Observation Network layer: its buoys report observed wave height at their exact locations, while this layer shows the wave model everywhere. How the buoys measure it: significant wave height (WVHT) is the average of the highest one-third of the waves recorded during a 20-minute sampling period each hour. Accelerometers on the hull record its heave motion, an onboard FFT converts that motion into a wave-energy spectrum, and the height is derived from that spectrum; buoy reports cover combined wind waves and swell. Great Lakes buoys are seasonal and are hauled out before ice season, so winter gaps are normal.</p><p><b>Status:</b> LIVE / CURRENT MODEL (analysis)</p><p><b>Source:</b> NOAA/NCEP Great Lakes Wave Unstructured v2.1 (GLWUv2.1, WAVEWATCH III)<br/><a href="https://nomads.ncep.noaa.gov/pub/data/nccf/com/glwu/prod/glwu.20261010/glwu.grlc_2p5km.t13z.grib2">https://nomads.ncep.noaa.gov/pub/data/nccf/com/glwu/prod/glwu.20261010/glwu.grlc_2p5km.t13z.grib2</a></p><p>Transparent outside valid water data so existing project layers (shipwrecks, lighthouses, harbors, parks) stay visible. Turn on/off independently of temperature and ice layers.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p>]]></description>
    <GroundOverlay>
      <name>🌊 LIVE WAVE HEIGHT</name>
      <drawOrder>10</drawOrder>
      <Icon>
        <href>https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/wave_height/current.png?v=glwu-20261010-1300Z-r12</href>
        <refreshMode>onInterval</refreshMode>
        <refreshInterval>900</refreshInterval>
      </Icon>
      <LatLonBox>
        <north>49.5</north>
        <south>40.5</south>
        <east>-73.5</east>
        <west>-93.0</west>
      </LatLonBox>
    </GroundOverlay>
  </Document>
